    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Well, Megan, I would not have in terms of actually raising an objection and saying that, listen, I think that what happened in Pennsylvania was wrong. I think that we need to have a debate about election integrity, which we're having now, by the way, because the Democrats in our proposing to change all of these state laws in one fell swoop. They were trying to do it state by state. Now they want to do it all at once. I think we needed to have that debate on January 6. I think we need to have it now. So in terms of my own my own objection on that day and doing what I did to represent the views of my constituents, I wouldn't change that. Now, you know, obviously, I think that to your point about anticipating a riot, I mean, did I think there was going to be a riot? Heck, no, I did not. And that's why I say that I've got zero sympathy for anybody who rioted for whatever reason they rioted for. And you know, you're certainly not going to know what's going to elicit any sympathy for any rioters for me, whether again, it's whether it's the people on January 6 or whether it's the deranged psycho who killed the cop at the Capitol a few weeks ago, or whether it's rioters in the streets to Portland or elsewhere. Whatever, if you break the law on assault cops, you're going to jail or you should.",
