    "turn_idx": 154,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I wouldn't change that part of it, Megan. I think that the basic premise, what 230 was written to do, at least in part, was to say that if there's truly third-party content, like you've just type out the size, you've got third-party content on the platform and the platform doesn't post it or the platform rather doesn't change it. It's just acting as a kind of a bulletin board, then you can't sue the platform for it, unless it's illegal, right? And they should know it's",
